## Milestone Rules

Looking at the chat messages in the screenshots, I can read the actual world coordinates. The commands show blocks placed around **(-3004, 72-73, -5569)**. Since commands use `~` relative coordinates from spawn, and the door is at `~6 ~1 ~4` while the campfire is at `~6 ~1 ~8`, I can establish the spawn-relative positions precisely.

Key observations from the sandbox:
- The door at `~6 ~1 ~4` is clearly visible from spawn (confirmed in all frames)
- The campfire at `~6 ~1 ~8` is enclosed inside the cabin, only visible after approaching/entering through the door
- The cabin walls fully enclose the interior, enforcing the spatial dependency

